%erg v1
Title: Drop .wip files and claim/release — WIP is not the spec's concern
Created: 2026-05-01
Author: claude
Status: open

--- log ---
2026-05-01T16:50Z claude created — proposal to remove .wip mechanism and the claim/release portion of 0006

--- body ---
## Idea

Remove `.git/ticket-wip/{ID}.wip` files and the `claim`/`release` commands
planned in 0006. The ticket spec should describe what a ticket *is*, not
how concurrent agents coordinate access to one.

## Rationale

- **WIP is observable out of band.** If a branch with the ticket ID in its
  name exists (locally or on a remote), the ticket is being worked on. That
  signal is enough — no parallel index needs to be maintained.
- **Branch-naming for coordination is not the spec's business.** Any
  convention (`feature/0042-foo`, `claude/0042-bar`, etc.) is a workflow
  choice between agents/humans, not a property of `%erg v1`. The spec
  should stay silent on it.
- **The mere possibility of out-of-band coordination is sufficient.** Even
  if no convention is followed, the absence of a `.wip` file does not
  prove "not WIP" — agents may forget to claim. So `.wip` was never a
  reliable lock; deleting it loses no real guarantee.
- **Aligns with 0012.** Same philosophy: derive state from observable
  facts, drop bookkeeping headers and side-files.

## Actions

1. Remove the WIP-cleanup branch from `cmdClose` in
   `tickets/tools/go/main.go` (the `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` block
   that deletes `ticket-wip/{ID}.wip`).
2. Drop `claim` and `release` from the action list in 0006; rescope 0006
   to the modularization + godoc work that remains.
3. Update `rules/tickets.md` to remove any `.wip` / `claim` / `release`
   references. Do **not** add a branch-naming convention — the spec stays
   silent on coordination.
4. Delete `.git/ticket-wip/` if it exists in any worktree (housekeeping,
   not committed).

## Out of scope

- Any branch-naming convention or "WIP detector" command. Stale-branch
  hygiene and remote-branch handling are user concerns, not the spec's.
- Status enum changes (covered by 0012).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `cmdClose` no longer touches `.git/ticket-wip/`
- [ ] 0006 rescoped (claim/release removed from its actions)
- [ ] `rules/tickets.md` makes no mention of `.wip` / claim / release
- [ ] Validator passes on all tickets
